messages.reasoning_content:
So `PyArray_NewFromDescr`/`PyArray_NewFromDescrAndBase` **steals a reference to descr**. On failure, descr is decref'd inside `PyArray_NewFromDescr_int`. In `PyArray_FromInterface` fail path:

```c
ret = (PyArrayObject *)PyArray_NewFromDescrAndBase(
        &PyArray_Type, dtype,
        n, dims, NULL, data,
        dataflags, NULL, base);
if (ret == NULL) {
    goto fail;
}
```

If `PyArray_NewFromDescrAndBase` returns NULL, it has already decref'd dtype (stolen reference). Then `goto fail` reaches `Py_XDECREF(dtype)` which decrefs the cached dtype AGAIN — double decrement!

This is indeed a bug for the path where NewFromDescr fails. For invalid shape/strides metadata? Hmm, invalid shape is detected before NewFromDescr is called, but invalid strides... wait:

Strides parsing happens after ret is created. Let me re-read the strides section:

```c
    attr = PyDict_GetItemString(iface, "strides");
    if (attr != NULL && attr != Py_None) {
        if (!PyTuple_Check(attr)) {
            ... goto fail;  // with Py_DECREF(ret) first
        }
        if (n != PyTuple_GET_SIZE(attr)) {
            ... Py_DECREF(ret); goto fail;
        }
        for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            PyObject *tmp = PyTuple_GET_ITEM(attr, i);
            strides[i] = PyArray_PyIntAsIntp(tmp);
            if (error_converting(strides[i])) {
                Py_DECREF(ret);
                goto fail;
            }
        }
        ...
    }
